# Regression: `Set[P] s = {}` (empty literal) failed C-compile pre-Round XXIV
# Track E with "incompatible types when assigning to type 'GorgetSet' from
# type 'int32_t'". Root: `collections.rs:277`'s
# `elem_size = infer_collection_element_type(ctx, Set__P)` fell back to
# `I64_TYPE` because `infer_collection_element_type` had no `Set__`/`HashSet__`
# arm — the empty-literal path handed a wrong-typed `SizeOf` operand to
# `gorget_set_new`, and the C-emit typed the returned local as `int32_t`
# instead of `GorgetSet`.
#
# Fix: extend `infer_collection_element_type` (Round XXIV Track E) with
# Set__/HashSet__ arms (arm-count lint bumped 5 → 7). Struct-payload cell.
# See TODO.md layering rule-2 debt entry for the reference-grade typed-field
# fix that remains queued.
#
# Set/HashSet REQUIRE `@derive(Equatable, Hashable)` on the payload
# (`E_UnsatisfiedTraitBound` otherwise).
@derive(Equatable, Hashable)
struct P:
    int x
    int y
    int z

int main():
    Set[P] s = {}
    s.add(P(1, 2, 3))
    s.add(P(4, 5, 6))
    for p in s:
        print(f"{p.x}/{p.y}/{p.z}")
    return 0
